      "source": [
        "# Look-Ahead-Free Market Regime Detection for Indian Equities\n",
        "### An early-warning signal for risk management and allocation\n",
        "\n",
        "**Problem statement.** Can we detect stressed conditions in Indian equities *in real time* — using only information available on each day — early enough to reduce drawdowns and make risk limits more reliable? And how much do the usual regime-detection setups overstate their own performance?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Research questions**\n",
        "- **RQ1 – Look-ahead gap:** How much does the typical setup (full-sample fit + smoothed probabilities) overstate performance versus a strict walk-forward, filtered-probability setup?\n",
        "- **RQ2 – India-specific features:** Do India VIX, market breadth, sector dispersion, USD/INR and Bank Nifty relative strength improve regime detection beyond returns and volatility alone?\n",
        "- **RQ3 – Early warning:** How quickly (and with how many false alarms) does each method flag ≥10% Nifty drawdowns?\n",
        "- **RQ4 – Risk application:** Does a regime-conditioned VaR give breach rates closer to target than static and EWMA VaR?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Honest-evaluation rules followed throughout**\n",
        "1. Every feature uses trailing data only. A decision made at the close of day *t* earns the return of day *t+1*.\n",
        "2. The HMM is refit every month on a rolling window, standardised with training-window statistics only.\n",
        "3. Regime probabilities are **filtered** (forward algorithm), never smoothed, in the main model.\n",
        "4. Every model is compared with simple baselines (buy-and-hold, India VIX rule, 200-DMA, volatility targeting), with transaction costs."
      ]
    },
