      "source": [
        "### 5.2 The 'typical notebook' versions (for RQ1)\n",
        "- **(A) Full-sample fit + smoothed probabilities:** what most tutorials do. Both the parameters and the probabilities see the future.\n",
        "- **(B) Full-sample fit + filtered probabilities:** the probabilities are causal, but the parameters are still fit on future data.\n",
        "- **(C) Walk-forward fit + filtered probabilities:** the main model (Section 5.1).\n",
        "\n",
        "The A→B gap is the cost of smoothing. The B→C gap is the cost of parameter look-ahead."
      ]
    },
