      "source": [
        "## 6. Allocation strategies and baselines (out of sample, after costs)\n",
        "\n",
        "Equity weight *w* is set at the close of day *t* and earns day *t+1*'s Nifty return. The rest of the portfolio is in cash at an assumed fixed yield (or in gold, for one variant). Costs = `COST_BPS` × |change in *w*|.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Strategy | Rule |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| Buy & hold | w = 1 |\n",
        "| India VIX rule | w = 0 if VIX > its expanding 80th percentile |\n",
        "| 200-DMA | w = 1 if Nifty > 200-day average |\n",
        "| Vol targeting | w = min(1, target vol / realised vol) |\n",
        "| HMM (prob-weighted) | w = 1 − EMA(P(stress)) |\n",
        "| HMM (hard switch) | risk-off when EMA(P) > 0.6, back on when < 0.4 |"
      ]
    },
