      "source": [
        "## 9. Regime-conditioned VaR (RQ4)\n",
        "**Regime VaR:** tomorrow's return is a mixture of state-conditional normal distributions, weighted by the *predicted* state probabilities P(s<sub>t+1</sub>) = filtered P(s<sub>t</sub>) × transition matrix. The 99% VaR is the 1% quantile of that mixture.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Baselines:** 500-day historical simulation, 252-day normal, and EWMA (RiskMetrics, λ = 0.94).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Kupiec POF test:** checks whether the breach rate equals 1%. A p-value above 0.05 means the model is not rejected."
      ]
    },
