        "## 12. Limitations and next steps\n",
        "- **Survivorship bias:** the breadth universe is a current large-cap list. Using point-in-time Nifty 50 membership would fix this.\n",
        "- **Price index, not total return:** Nifty dividends (roughly 1–1.5% a year) are excluded for every strategy. This slightly understates buy-and-hold and the equity legs alike.\n",
        "- **Fixed cash yield and cost assumptions:** the results are sensitive to `COST_BPS` and `CASH_YIELD`. Rerun with different values.\n",
        "- **yfinance data quality:** occasional gaps and spikes, especially in USD/INR and older India VIX data.\n",
        "- **Multiple testing:** several configurations were tried. A Deflated Sharpe Ratio would be the rigorous correction.\n",
        "- **Next steps (research paper):** test whether US stress regimes (`^VIX`) *lead* Indian regime shifts; add FII/DII flow data from NSE; run robustness checks over refit windows, 2 vs 3 states, and sub-periods.\n",
      ]
    }
